[38;2;124;124;124mIf $a/T$ is irrational, then the set $\{ka \mod T : k \in \mathbb{Z}\}$ is dense[0m[38;2;124;124;124min $[0, T)$. Since $f(x + ka) = f(x) - kc/2$ and $f$ is $T$-periodic, $f(x + ka [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\mod T) = f(x) - kc/2$ (where we reduce $ka$ mod $T$). As $k$ varies, $ka \mod [0m
